# Files Vercel should not upload or build.
#
# api/ — the FastAPI backend.
#
# Vercel treats a root-level `api/` directory as serverless functions by
# convention, so every deploy was installing api/requirements.txt and shipping
# a second, unconfigured copy of the backend as a Python lambda:
#
#     Installing required dependencies from api/requirements.txt...
#
# That copy has no SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, so it can't reach the database
# and does nothing — but it burns build minutes and is a live endpoint nobody
# is watching. The real backend deploys separately to Render (Root Directory
# `api`), which reads the folder straight from GitHub and is unaffected by
# this file.
api/

# Local Python artifacts, in case they ever escape .gitignore.
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/

# Legacy standalone HTML from the pre-Next.js site (~3.5 MB of it). Kept in the
# repo for visual reference; no reason to ship it to the CDN.
*standalone*.html
portfolio-html.html
